### Session 19 — test the Products API directly
### In VS Code, install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request".
### The app prints its URL on `dotnet run` (e.g. http://localhost:5000).
### You normally use the web page (../frontend/index.html) as the client,
### but these let you test the API on its own.

@base = http://localhost:5000

### 1) GET all products
GET {{base}}/api/products

### 2) GET one product by id
GET {{base}}/api/products/1

### 3) CREATE a new product -> 201
POST {{base}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Headphones",
  "price": 59.90,
  "description": "Over-ear, noise cancelling."
}

### 4) UPDATE product 1 -> 204
PUT {{base}}/api/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Blue Pen",
  "price": 3.50,
  "description": "A smooth blue ballpoint pen."
}

### 5) DELETE product 2 -> 204
DELETE {{base}}/api/products/2
